## Done — Tetris in Rust + ratatui

Built at `/home/gud/bench-harnesses/results/27b-qwen-2/tetris/`.

**Run it:**
```sh
cd /home/gud/bench-harnesses/results/27b-qwen-2/tetris
cargo run            # or: cargo run --release
```

**Controls:** `←`/`→` move · `↓` soft drop · `↑`/`X` rotate CW · `Z` rotate CCW · `Space` hard drop · `P` pause · `R` restart · `Q`/`Esc` quit

**Structure** (822 lines):
- `src/tetromino.rs` — the 7 pieces, SRS-style box rotation, guideline colors
- `src/game.rs` — board, collision, 7-bag randomizer, line clearing, scoring/levels, gravity (+ 6 unit tests)
- `src/main.rs` — event loop, board/sidebar rendering, ghost piece, pause & game-over overlays
- `Cargo.toml` (ratatui 0.30, crossterm 0.29), `README.md`

**Features:** SRS-style rotation with wall kicks, ghost piece, score + in-session high score, level/lines with speed-up (10 lines/level), next-piece preview, pause, and game-over/restart.

**Verification:**
- ✅ `cargo build` (debug) and `cargo build --release` — no errors
- ✅ `cargo clippy --all-targets` — clean, zero warnings
- ✅ `cargo test` — **6/6 passed** (rotation stays in box, out-of-bounds rejected, single-line clear + scoring, hard-drop completing two rows, 7-bag deals all seven pieces)
